-- SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
-- Ordinary meanings and practical facets. These are explanations, not game
-- recipes, live observations or executable commands. No external dictionary.
-- Sealed food: USDA FSIS, How long can you keep canned goods? (2026-11-15).
-- Charcoal: CPSC, Charcoal safety information centre (2026-11-15).
SurvivorCompanion=SurvivorCompanion or {}
SurvivorCompanion.EmmaMeaningData={
 {id="advisory",terms={"advisory","notice"},what="An advisory is a notice giving information or guidance about a situation. An old county advisory is not proof of a current alert."},
 {id="offline",terms={"offline","disconnected","unavailable"},what="Offline means a service is unavailable or disconnected. I cannot fetch a current map through an offline map service, and that word alone does not tell us the cause or a repair time."},
 {id="combination",terms={"combination"},context={"lock","cabinet","code"},what="A lock combination is the correct sequence of numbers or symbols used to open it. Knowing what a combination means does not tell us the actual code."},
 {id="reserve",terms={"reserve"},what="A reserve is a supply kept back for later or for an emergency. Its purpose does not establish how much is actually stored."},
 {id="spare",terms={"spare","backup"},what="A spare is an extra item kept as a backup if the main one is lost, used up or fails.",why="The spare is a backup if your main light fails or its batteries run out. That is a reason to carry one, not a reading of either light's charge."},
 {id="backup_copy",terms={"backup"},context={"copy","notes","record","file"},what="A backup is an additional copy kept in case the original is lost or damaged. Keep it separate where possible; discussing it has not created a copy."},
 {id="load",terms={"load","carrying","carry","bag","packing","supplies"},context={"supplies","run","pile","trip","carry","bag","stay"},what="The load is the supplies or weight you are carrying. Choose an amount you can manage and still move comfortably.",how="Use a suitable bag or container if one is available. Otherwise carry small manageable loads by hand and make more than one trip. What carrying space do you have?",alternative="Without a bag, use another suitable container if available, or carry a smaller load by hand and make repeated trips. I have not found or equipped a bag for you."},
 {id="manual",terms={"manual","instructions"},what="A manual gives instructions for the equipment: suitable fuel or power, operation, maintenance and warnings. Check the actual model's manual; I have not opened a particular copy here."},
 {id="funnel",terms={"funnel"},affinity={"pour","oil","liquid","transfer"},what="A funnel has a wide mouth narrowing to a small outlet. It helps pour liquid into a smaller opening with fewer spills; choose one suitable for the liquid.",alternative="Without a funnel, a suitable pouring spout or smaller compatible vessel may give you more control. If you cannot transfer it safely, get a suitable funnel first. Keep flames away from fuel or lamp oil; nothing has been poured here."},
 {id="spoilage",terms={"spoilage","spoiling","spoiled"},what="Food spoilage means food deteriorating or going off. Time and unsuitable storage can contribute. That definition does not establish the condition of any particular food."},
 {id="fallback",terms={"fallback"},what="A fallback is a backup plan. An agreed meeting place tells people where to gather if they become separated or the original plan fails."},
 {id="cache",terms={"cache","cached"},what="A cache is a saved or stored copy kept for reuse. A cached map can be old; finding that word in a record does not confirm retrieval or current accuracy."},
 {id="fuel_container",terms={"fuel","gasoline","petrol","fuel can","tank"},context={"storage","container","can","holds","spare","move","generator"},what="Store spare fuel in a suitable fuel-rated can or container, with its proper closure. An ordinary drinking bottle is not a substitute. I am not assuming you own a fuel can."},
 {id="can_opener",terms={"can opener","opener","tins"},context={"tin","tins","lid","food","beans"},what="A pull-tab tin may open with its tab. Other tins need a suitable can opener. Check the actual lid and the tools you have; I do not know which kind these are.",alternative="Check whether a tin has a usable pull tab. If it needs an opener, find a suitable one or choose other accessible food for now. I am not assuming an opener is available."},
 {id="light",terms={"light","lamp","torch","flashlight","lantern","candle"},what="A battery lamp uses its own batteries and can work independently of building mains electricity. A torch or flashlight is another portable light. What equipment and power source do you have?",how="For lighting a room without mains power, use a suitable torch, flashlight or battery lamp if one is available. What equipment and power source do you have?",diagnose="Check the power switch, how the batteries are seated and the contacts. Use the correct replacement batteries if available. A failed torch is not proof that its battery is dead; what type of torch and battery is it?",find="For indoor light, use a suitable torch, flashlight or battery lamp if available. What power source or lighting equipment do you actually have?",packing="Candles can provide light if you also have matches or a lighter and a stable suitable holder. Keep them dry and away from things that can burn. I have not assumed any are packed."},
 {id="candles",terms={"candle","candles"},context={"flame","burn","burns"},what="Candles provide light with a flame. Keep them attended in a stable suitable holder, away from material that burns. This is a fire precaution, not a report that any candle is lit."},
 {id="sealed_food",terms={"beans","tins","cans","tinned","canned"},context={"sealed","unopened","intact"},what="Intact sealed tins belong in a cool, clean, dry place such as a pantry shelf. Keep them away from excessive heat and damp. Opened food has different storage needs; this advice does not certify damaged tins.",how="Keep those sealed tins on a cool, clean, dry shelf or in a pantry. They do not need to be treated as opened beans. Inspect the containers; damaged or suspect tins need separate attention."},
 {id="firewood",terms={"firewood","wood","stove"},context={"wood","stove","burns","fuel"},what="For a wood-burning stove, use suitable dry or seasoned wood in pieces that fit the stove. Wet wood is harder to burn well. Check the stove's instructions and ventilation; no supply of wood is assumed."},
 {id="rain_collection",terms={"rain","collector","collectors","catchment"},what="A rain collector receives rain in a container or from a catchment and stores it. It needs to be outdoors where rain can enter; it does not fill merely because it exists.",how="Put a suitable open container outdoors where rain can enter and wait for rain. Keep it stable and protect the stored water from dirt. This does not mean it is raining now or that any water has been collected; drinking water needs its own safety checks."},
 {id="boards",terms={"planks","boards","bundle"},context={"plank","planks","boards","carry","bag"},what="Long boards can be awkward to carry even when they are not very heavy.",how="If practical, tie the boards into a stable manageable bundle and carry them by hand. Smaller loads or repeated trips may be easier. Keep the ends clear of people and obstacles; I have not moved them."},
 {id="tools",terms={"tools","repair tools"},find="Garages, workshops, sheds and hardware shops are plausible places to search for basic tools. Check the approach and actual shelves; I cannot promise nearby stock or an open shop."},
 {id="grill",terms={"grill","grilling","charcoal"},what="Use a charcoal grill outdoors in an open, well-ventilated place with clearance from things that can burn. Never use it inside a room or garage; charcoal produces carbon monoxide.",find="Grill outdoors in open air, away from things that can burn. Do not use an enclosed room, garage or a combustible overhang. I cannot inspect the proposed spot for you."},
 {id="battery",terms={"battery","batteries","power switch"},what="A battery stores energy for a device. Its presence does not establish its remaining charge.",how="Switch the lamp or radio off when it is not needed, and reduce unnecessary brightness or use where the controls allow it. This conserves energy; I have not measured the charge or operated the controls."},
 {id="ties",terms={"rope","cord","tie","boxes"},context={"boxes","box","bundle","carry","together"},what="Rope or cord can hold items together as a bundle.",how="Wrap suitable rope around the boxes and tie a secure, stable bundle you can manage. Check that the boxes do not slip and the load is not too heavy. Discussing it has not tied or moved anything."},
 {id="rust",terms={"rust","rusting"},what="Rust is corrosion of iron: iron reacts with oxygen and moisture. It changes the metal at the surface; the amount of damage still needs inspection.",why="Iron rusts when it reacts with oxygen and moisture. That explains the process, not the extent of damage to this particular object."},
 {id="staling",terms={"stale","staling","bread"},context={"bread","uncovered","texture"},what="Stale bread has changed texture over time as moisture moves and its starch structure changes. Uncovered bread can also dry out. Staleness is not the same finding as mould.",why="Bread becomes stale as its starch structure and moisture distribution change over time. Left uncovered it can also lose moisture and dry out. That is about texture, not a diagnosis of mould or illness."},
 {id="wind_power",terms={"wind","turbine"},context={"electricity","power","generator","blades"},what="Wind turns a turbine's blades, which drive a generator to make electricity. Whether it can supply a particular device depends on the equipment and wind; none is assumed installed here.",how="Moving air turns turbine blades, and that motion drives a generator. The electrical output depends on the installation and wind; I have not measured or connected one."},
 {id="radio_hiss",terms={"hiss","hissing","static"},context={"radio","stations","receiver"},what="Radio hiss is static or noise from the receiver, often most noticeable without a clear tuned signal. It does not by itself identify a transmitter or a message.",why="Between stations, a receiver can amplify background noise instead of a clear signal, producing hiss or static. Tuning and reception may matter; I cannot diagnose an exact fault from that alone."},
 {id="wet_weight",terms={"wet","soaked","heavier"},context={"coat","fabric","clothing","cloth"},what="Water retained in fabric adds to its weight.",why="The wet coat holds water in its fabric, and that water adds weight. That explains why the same coat can be heavier soaked than dry."},
 {id="security",terms={"lock","locking","locked"},proposal=true,context={"shed","tools","door","access"},why="Locking the shed can help keep tools from being taken or accessed without permission. It is a barrier, not a guarantee of security, and I have not locked it."},
 {id="dry",terms={"dry","damp"},context={"matches","container","rain","moisture"},what="Dry means free of unwanted water or damp. Keep matches away from rain and moisture, for example in a suitable covered container or dry cupboard; I have not checked their condition."},
 {id="estimate",terms={"estimate","approximate"},what="An estimate is an approximation based on available information. Estimated travel time is not a guaranteed arrival time or a current clock reading."},
 {id="switch",terms={"switch"},context={"lamp","power","light"},what="The switch is the lamp's physical power control. Look for the control on the actual lamp; I do not know its precise model or operate it remotely."},
 {id="log",terms={"log","paper log"},context={"paper","written","supplies","record"},what="A paper log is a written record. For supplies, list the items, quantities and changes as things are used or replaced. This means a record, not a timber log or a computer command."},
 {id="boots",terms={"boots","boot","shoes"},what="Wet boots need drying with airflow rather than intense direct heat.",how="Remove the insoles if they are removable, loosen the boots and let air circulate. Dry paper inside can take up moisture; replace it as it gets damp. Avoid intense direct heat, and do not assume an exact drying time."},
 {id="screws",terms={"screws","screw","fasteners"},what="Screws can differ in length, diameter and head type.",how="Sort the screws by length, size and head type. Put each group in a separate container or labelled pile so similar fasteners stay together. The sorting has not been performed here."},
 {id="map",terms={"map","atlas"},context={"paper","wet","pocket","rain"},what="A paper map needs protection from water.",how="Put the map in a waterproof pouch or suitable sealed plastic bag if available, or a better protected inside pocket. Keep it dry; I have not repaired or replaced it."},
 {id="echo",terms={"echo","echoes"},what="An echo is sound reflected by a surface and heard again.",why="Sound reflects from hard surfaces such as concrete walls and returns to you, creating an echo. It need not be another person answering or a received radio signal."},
 {id="pulley",terms={"pulley","pulleys"},what="A pulley guides a rope over a wheel and can change the direction of a pull.",how="With a rope over a fixed pulley, pulling down can lift the load up. That changes direction; a single fixed pulley does not automatically reduce the force. Some pulley arrangements trade more rope travel for less force."},
 {id="hinge",terms={"hinge","squeak","squeaks"},what="A hinge lets a door turn around a pivot.",why="A hinge can squeak from friction, dirt or poor lubrication. Inspect it and use a suitable hinge lubricant if needed; the sound does not prove a particular unseen defect or completed repair."},
 {id="wooden_drawer",terms={"drawer","sticking","binding"},context={"wooden","wood","sticking"},what="A sticking wooden drawer may be binding against its frame or catching an obstruction.",how="Do not force the drawer. Check gently for an obstruction or where the wood binds; a suitable dry sliding aid may help if the construction allows it. What part catches? I have not opened or diagnosed the drawer."},
}
